  <div class="page">
    <h1 class="page-title">About Nikhil Singhal</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I'm Nikhil Singhal, an AI-first builder and architect. I ship consumer and enterprise products built on agents, retrieval and edge AI. My first AI product took nine months. My most recent took a day.</p>
      <p>Recent client work, through <a href="https://omspark.com">OmSpark</a>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>An agentic enterprise search platform for a large enterprise client</li>
        <li>A property tax appeals platform that runs millions of parcels through a 15-step pipeline and 33 agent gates</li>
        <li>Production engineering for ParkPro, an on-demand truck parking platform</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I'm going deep on human intent and AI: the gap between what a person means and what the machine does. AI Trust Commons is where I do that work. <a href="/">The picture on the home page</a> shows what that looks like inside a company.</p>
      <p>The same thread runs through:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://centereye.ai">CenterEye</a>, that idea built as a product. It's the system of record for your rules, decisions and open work. Claude, ChatGPT, Grok and Gemini all read and write to it.</li>
        <li><a href="/hip-charter/">The Human Intelligence Partnership Charter</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/">From Instinct to Intent™</a>, my article series</li>
        <li>A <a href="https://www.regulations.gov/comment/NIST-2025-0035-0424">public comment to NIST</a> on AI agent governance, and a <a href="/blog/2026/03/23/nccoe-ai-agent-identity-authorization-response/">response to its NCCoE paper</a> on agent identity and authorization</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Three decades of building came before the AI: enterprise scale at Microsoft, Expedia and T-Mobile, and startups where I served as CTO. That work meant meeting compliance rules in seven industries. Healthcare and telecom were two of them. I've led teams of over 200 across product, engineering and design. Seattle, WA.</p>
      <h2>Published work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18917473">Discovering Intent</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18917473)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19005877">Languages Designed for Humans</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19005877)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19025149">Engine vs Steering Wheel</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19025149)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19079578">Stop Calling It Artificial</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19079578)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19187738">Discovering Humanity Through AI</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19187738)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19078843">The Human Intelligence Partnership Charter</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19078843)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18903117">NIST public comment on AI agent governance</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18903117)</li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19197399">NCCoE response: intent conveyance in AI agent authorization</a> (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19197399)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I take on advisory and contract work through <a href="https://omspark.com">OmSpark</a>. Email <a href="mailto:nikhil@omspark.com">nikhil@omspark.com</a>.</p>
      <p><a href="https://nikhilsinghal.com">nikhilsinghal.com</a> · <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/nikhilsinghal">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://github.com/nikhilsi">GitHub</a> · <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5449-6830">ORCID</a> · <a href="mailto:nikhil@aitrustcommons.org">Email</a></p>
    </div>
